2. Job Research
    Primary Role – Report Writer
    
    Purpose of the Role
    A Report Writer prepares professional business documents that communicate information clearly to managers, clients and stakeholders.
    The role involves collecting information, analysing data and producing reports that support business decisions.

    Common Responsibilities
    Responsibility	        Description
    Write reports	        Prepare business, technical and project reports
    Collect information	    Gather information from stakeholders and systems
    Analyse data	        Review data before writing reports
    Edit documents	        Ensure grammar, formatting and consistency
    Meet deadlines	        Produce reports within required timeframes
    Work with teams	        Communicate with project managers and business staff
    
    
    Secondary Role – Business Analyst
    
    Purpose of the Role
    A Business Analyst helps organisations improve business processes by identifying business needs and recommending technology or process improvements.

    Common Responsibilities
    Responsibility	            Description
    Gather requirements	        Meet stakeholders and identify business needs
    Analyse business processes	Find areas for improvement
    Create documentation	    Write Business Requirements Documents (BRDs)
    Produce process diagrams	Document workflows using diagrams
    Support projects	        Work with developers and testers
    Validate solutions	        Ensure business requirements are met

    Business Analyst positions in Darwin commonly request experience with stakeholder engagement, documentation, process mapping and business systems.

